    // Replace with the permission appropriate for your chosen foreground service type
    SDL_RequestAndroidPermission("android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_YOUR_FOREGROUND_SERVICE_TYPE", permissionCallback, nullptr);
#endif



How it works
When you set SDL_HINT_ANDROID_FORCE_FOREGROUND_SERVICE to "1", the SDL Android backend performs the following actions on your behalf: 
It creates and manages a standard Android Service.
It uses the Context.startForegroundService() method to start the service.
It calls ServiceCompat.startForeground() inside the service, which requires a persistent notification. SDL handles the notification display. 
This process keeps your SDL application running even if it is moved to the background, preventing the OS from pausing or stopping your process.
